      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. This is because they are running a tactical proof of concept (PoC) of NoiseGuard, a competitor positioned as a low-mid pricing tactical noise reduction tool. There is a high retention risk if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, as procurement is likely to extend NoiseGuard and reduce Northstar's scope. This risk is explicitly noted in the competitor report for Pioneer Freight Solutions.\n\nThe exact next promised milestone for Pioneer Freight Solutions is the verification of schema registry compatibility and collection of the taxonomy snapshot, due on 2026-03-22. This milestone is part of the agreed remediation plan to address the taxonomy change incident impacting search relevance and entity graph linking.\n\nAdditional context includes subsequent milestones such as building a shadow index (2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09), backfill enrichment and recompute index weights (2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30), and a validation window (2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14). However, the immediate next milestone is the schema registry verification and taxonomy snapshot collection due 2026-03-22.\n\nThe competitive risk is that NoiseGuard is perceived as a cheaper near-term fix, and if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, procurement may favor NoiseGuard, which is a tactical competitor with strengths in easy deployment and low operational overhead but weaknesses in deeper automation and compliance tooling that Northstar offers.\n\nNo evidence is available about other customers' likelihood to defect to cheaper tactical competitors if milestones are missed, so it cannot be confirmed if Pioneer Freight Solutions is uniquely the most likely. Also, no explicit ranking or comparison of likelihood to defect among customers is provided, so the assertion that Pioneer Freight Solutions is the most likely is based on the explicit risk statement but 