      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern affecting multiple Canadian accounts after migration from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product, not just MapleBridge Insurance. The affected customers with this pattern are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleBridge Insurance, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, and MapleWest Bank.\n\nThe shared failure pattern is that after migration, approval workflows for region-specific (Canada) policies fail due to incorrect rule evaluation precedence. Specifically, global-default rules are incorrectly overriding or bypassing Canada-specific or province-specific approval rules because of rule evaluation order bugs, schema normalization mismatches (such as 'country_code' vs 'country'), or delayed schema registry synchronization. This causes approval playbooks to skip approver nodes, approvals to be stuck or auto-denied, approvals routed to global approvers instead of Canada approvers, or Canada-specific approval gating to be bypassed.\n\nIn plain English: after migrating to the new approval system, the rules that should ensure Canadian-specific approvals are required are being overridden by more general global rules. This leads to approvals being bypassed or stuck, misrouted approvals, missing audit entries, and gaps in compliance evidence.\n\nMapleBridge Insurance is not a one-off case; it is part of this broader recurring pattern affecting multiple Canadian customers after migration.\n\nThis pattern is triggered by migration from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product and involves region-specific policy overrides failing due to rule precedence and schema normalization issues.\n\n[art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158, art_3db205cb21ca]",
